<p>So basically, my SCP is a Euclid class anomaly which is a muddy puddle. it's sort of like a cave system full of mud with a huge internal area. The trick is, every day, a few mud creatures come out of the hole and are aggressive to anyone that is nearby. They usually try to suffocate this person or in rare cases assimilate the person into themselves. Because of this danger, the SCP Foundation have set up a secure area around the SCP and armed MTF soldiers with incendiary devices (one of the only known weaknesses).<br />
Usually 2-3 monsters come out of the puddle a day, but in rainy/stormy weather, that number can be boosted to 10-30 monsters. That's why they keep meteorological scientists and researchers on-site.</p>
