						<a href="/forum/t-13930511/scp-idea-algernon-13">SCP Idea - Algernon-13</a>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4849312">
									

<p>I feel like I'd appreciate this concept more as a tale centred around like, five people at a remote research base who each experience this and like&#8230;react in different ways (think e.g. John Carpenter's The Thing in style); where the interesting thing is watching it unfold and everyone trying to figure out what's happening and what to do about this; and the star trying to communicate something say, with the piece ending on us discovering that and it being some kind of message that's like&#8230;shocking or surprising?</p>
<p>My concern with this as a SCP is that it feels like a lot of this would rely on like, really intimate character moments and very personal emotional states, and that kinda thing can be really hard to include in a SCP article in a way that doesn't feel out of place.</p>
<p>Even then though, my concern is that there's not quite enough here to make this really interesting: the actual effects feel&#8230;too compulsive and too powerful for the character interactions to really work. Specifically: because this doesn't give people a choice about what to do, and because they can't interact with others while they're doing it, them actually like&#8230;making something or drawing art isn't as impactful because there can't be a scene where someone is desperately trying to convey an idea that's like&#8230;far beyond their understanding. And it feels like that desperation is what would make this interesting.</p>

							</div>

								
					
